---
title: Griddled Venison with Pink Gin Apple Sauce and Roast Pencil Leeks
source: Nigella Express <urn:isbn:9780701181840>
author: Nigella Lawson
course: Main
servings: 6
prep time: 15m
cook time: 15m
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Medium
tags:
- savoury
- main-course
- meat
---

Put the @venison loin{750%g} into a large freezer bag and add the remaining ingredients (@gin{125%ml}, @Worcestershire sauce{2%tsp}, @olive oil{60%ml}, @black peppercorns{2%tsp}, @onion{1}(quartered), @star anise{2}, and @garlic cloves{2}(bruised)). Leave out for at least ~{20%minutes}, or if you can afford the time up to ~{2%hours}, or even overnight in the fridge.

Heat a #large griddle{} until almost smoking hot. Take the venison out of the marinade (discard the marinade), shaking it well, then slap down onto the hot griddle and cook for about ~{15%minutes}, turning frequently to give even scorch marks.

When the venison is ready, remove to a carving board to rest, loosely tented with foil, before slicing thinly. Serve with @./Savoury/Pink Gin Apple Sauce{} and @./Savoury/Roast Pencil Leeks{}.